==English==

===Etymology===
Coined by Paracelsus from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|συν-||with}} + {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|ovum||egg}} + {{m|la|-ia||}}, as synovia resembles the consistency and appearance of eggwhite.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The lubricating fluid secreted by the synovium of a joint or other such structure; usually called [[synovial fluid]].

